 "titulo": {
  "estudio": "Hoy he comido, ayer comí",
  "alumno": "Today I have eaten, yesterday I ate"
 },
 "intro": "Two ways to talk about the past. Time words help you choose, although usage changes by region.",
 "palabras": [
  {
   "palabra": "esta mañana",
   "significado": "this morning",
   "pron": "ES-ta ma-NYA-na",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "adverb",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "This morning is still part of today. That is why «esta mañana he desayunado» sounds natural in Spain.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "esta semana",
   "significado": "this week",
   "pron": "ES-ta se-MA-na",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "adverb",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "The current week includes today. In Spain it usually takes the perfecto: «esta semana he trabajado mucho».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "este año",
   "significado": "this year",
   "pron": "ES-te A-nyo",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "adverb",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "A year that has not ended is still open. You say «este año he viajado poco».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "alguna vez",
   "significado": "ever, at some point",
   "pron": "al-GU-na BETH",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "adverb",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It is used to ask about experiences: «¿Has comido paella alguna vez?». It is written as two words.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "nunca",
   "significado": "never",
   "pron": "NUN-ka",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "adverb",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "With the perfecto it goes before the verb: «nunca he ido». You do not need to add «no».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "ayer",
   "significado": "yesterday",
   "pron": "a-YER",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "adverb",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It is a finished day. That is why it takes the indefinido: «ayer comí pizza». The y sounds as in «yo».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "anoche",
   "significado": "last night",
   "pron": "a-NO-che",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "adverb",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It is one word: «anoche». It talks about a finished moment, so you say «anoche cené».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "el lunes pasado",
   "significado": "last Monday",
   "pron": "el LU-nes pa-SA-do",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "set expression",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It works with any day: «el martes pasado». It is a finished time, so use the indefinido.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "la semana pasada",
   "significado": "last week",
   "pron": "la se-MA-na pa-SA-da",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "set expression",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "«Pasada» agrees with «semana»: feminine. With «el año pasado» it is «pasado», masculine.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "el año pasado",
   "significado": "last year",
   "pron": "el A-nyo pa-SA-do",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "set expression",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "A year that has already closed. «Año» is written with ñ, which sounds «ny»: «el año pasado fui a Perú».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "hace un año",
   "significado": "a year ago",
   "pron": "A-the un A-nyo",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "set expression",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "«Hace» + time counts back from today: «hace dos meses». The h is silent and the c sounds «th».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "el otro día",
   "significado": "the other day",
   "pron": "el O-tro DI-a",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "set expression",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It does not say which day, but it is a finished past: «el otro día vi a Marta».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "he ido",
   "significado": "I have gone, I have been",
   "pron": "e I-do",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "verb",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "«Ir» has the participle «ido». With «nunca»: «nunca he ido a Perú».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "fui",
   "significado": "I went",
   "pron": "fwi",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "verb",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "«Fui» is also the indefinido of «ser». Context tells you which one: «fui al cine».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "viajado",
   "significado": "travelled (viajar)",
   "pron": "bya-HA-do",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "verb",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "Only the ending changes: «viajar» becomes «viajado».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "cené",
   "significado": "had dinner (cenar)",
   "pron": "the-NE",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "verb",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "The accent marks the past: «ceno» is now, «cené» is yesterday.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "leído",
   "significado": "read (leer)",
   "pron": "le-I-do",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "verb",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "The accent splits the vowels: «le-í-do», not «leido».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "rosada",
   "significado": "pink",
   "pron": "ro-SA-da",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "adjective",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It ends in -a because it describes the feminine noun «luz».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "tocado",
   "significado": "touched (tocar)",
   "pron": "to-KA-do",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "verb",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "The c before a sounds like k: «tocado».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "bar",
   "significado": "bar, small café",
   "pron": "BAR",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "noun",
   "genero": "m",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It is written like the English word, with a clear final r.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "arcoíris",
   "significado": "rainbow",
   "pron": "ar-ko-I-ris",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "noun",
   "genero": "m",
   "plural": "",
